      "evidence": "Industry classification systems (e.g., NAICS code 334111 – Electronic Computer Manufacturing) place laptops under “electronic computers and peripherals.”",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "No laptop model or manufacturer is listed in Fairtrade International’s certified‑product database.",
      "evidence": "A search of the publicly searchable Fairtrade International certified‑product database (accessed 2024‑07‑15) using keywords such as “laptop”, and major brand names (Dell, HP, Lenovo, Apple, ASUS, Acer, Framework, Fairphone) returns zero matches; Fairtrade International also confirms that electronics are not eligible for certification.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Because no laptop meets the Fairtrade certification criteria, a laptop cannot be purchased that is officially labeled as “Fair Trade”.",
      "evidence": "The Fairtrade label may only be applied to products that have been certified under the Fairtrade Standard; absence of certification means the label cannot be used legally on a laptop.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [3]
    }
  ],
